      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "UNMATCHED (2) sets the standard in a modest CL1 over this trip, bringing recent BM58 form that reads well for this. His fourth at Moruya was solid behind Peruno after racing handy, and the Bathurst run prior had some interference attached. Drawn well again and rates a leading hope. LIYAH'S GIRL (1) has the most attractive recent profile, winning Newcastle maiden before charging home hard into second here last time, though the big weight and wide barrier will make the task less straightforward. C'MON WICKSY (6) is harder to sell on winning habit but he's knocking on the door and gets in light as he's still a maiden. COURTING EMILY (4) needs to turn around two plain Newcastle runs, including defeat by LIYAH'S GIRL last time, but blinkers first time and weight relief give him a chance to improve sharply. Boudvillain's booking is another bonus. Expecting TORPEDO TED (7) to be handy again and if he brings his best he can cause a scare.",
